ontent.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1qmle27/bcbb773c-3fa9-4c0b-bc08-aea261c53eca/91eaaff0-b756-11ec-8ad4-0909082a0cae/file-1l1qmle28.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1qmle27/bcbb773c-3fa9-4c0b-bc08-aea261c53eca/91eaaff0-b756-11ec-8ad4-0909082a0cae/file-1l1qmle28.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1qmle27/bcbb773c-3fa9-4c0b-bc08-aea261c53eca/91eaaff0-b756-11ec-8ad4-0909082a0cae/file-1l1qmle28.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"preparation-properties-and-uses-of-carboxylic-acids","type":"mcq","year":2013,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l1nco06v","chapter":"thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pthe-succeeding-operations-that-enable-this-transformation-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-hrdbtxnxspzv2j9p","question":{"en":{"content":"<p>The succeeding operations that enable this transformation of states are</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Heating, cooling, heating, cooling."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Cooling, heating, cooling, heating."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Heating, cooling, cooling, heating."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cooling, heating, heating, cooling."}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>From the graph, as the term pV increases, the temperature increases; and when pV decreases the temperature decreases.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Thermodynamics Question 24 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The term PV increases K<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>L, so this involves heating and is an isobaric process.</p>\n<p>It increases from N<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>K, so this involves heating and is an isochoric process.</p>\n<p>It decreases from M<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>N, so this involves cooling and is an isobaric process.</p>\n<p>It decreases from L<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>M, so this involves cooling and is an isochoric process.</p>","comprehension":"<p>A fixed mass m of a gas is subjected to transformation of states from K to L to M to N and back to K as shown in the figure.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Thermodynamics Question 24 English Comprehension\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1qnpmuj/13587a15-dc69-4c03-b324-f703e1c4f1a3/f111fbb0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnpmuk.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"fundamentals-of-thermodynamics","type":"mcq","year":2013,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l1ncqh51","chapter":"thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pthe-pair-of-isochoric-processes-among-the-transformation-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-r3p9hofjugp1guvx","question":{"en":{"content":"<p>The pair of isochoric processes among the transformation of states is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"K to L and L to M"},{"identifier":"B","content":"L to M and N to K"},{"identifier":"C","content":"L to M and M to N"},{"identifier":"D","content":"M to N and N to K"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>From the above solution, we have</p>\n<p>From K<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>L : heating (isobaric)</p>\n<p>From L<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>M : cooling (isochoric)</p>\n<p>From M<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=